-and-tooling/rationale.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A first run on a new runner often fails for reasons outside the code; this way it fails while nothing is locked"}, {"id": "docs_specs_0002_standards_and_tooling_rationale_decision_32", "label": "Decision 32: Evidence after the merge reaches main through a second pull request from scope/<number>-closing (M2, heavy)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/0002-standards-and-tooling/rationale.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Merge and failing-PR addresses exist only after the merge; heavy because it replaces coordination skill step 9 for every later scope"}, {"id": "docs_specs_0002_standards_and_tooling_rationale_decision_33", "label": "Decision 33: Rule C3: short allowed key list, one-line run steps, known <name> (M4)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/0002-standards-and-tooling/rationale.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A few lines in the existing reader naming the bad key; the fuller W7-style comparison is kept as Follow-up 11"}, {"id": "docs_specs_0002_standards_and_tooling_rationale_decision_34", "label": "Decision 34: Allowed run: names are a job id of the file or tools", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/0002-standards-and-tooling/rationale.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A new job gets its name allowed by adding the job; C2 ties job ids to the branch rule"}, {"id": "docs_specs_0002_standards_and_tooling_rationale_decision_35", "label": "Decision 35: One-workflow-file and stricter permissions rules live inside C5 (m16, m17)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/0002-standards-and-tooling/rationale.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "0002 AC-7 names C1 to C5; a C6 would change criterion text for no gain"}, {"id": "docs_specs_0002_standards_and_tooling_rationale_decision_36", "label": "Decision 36: W5 keeps reading manifests with the four spellings added (M3)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/0002-standards-and-tooling/rationale.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same helper removes m13 false alarms; Cargo.lock edges option is Follow-up 10"}, {"id": "docs_specs_0002_standards_and_tooling_rationale_decision_37", "label": "Decision 37: Sources half proven by a real Git dependency in a temporary folder (m11)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/0002-standards-and-tooling/rationale.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only a case that leaves deny.toml alone can catch a later edit weakening unknown-git"}, {"id": "docs_specs_0002_standards_and_tooling_rationale_decision_38", "label": "Decision 38: Remaining guard gaps named as known limits (m14, m15, m17-m19)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/0002-standards-and-tooling/rationale.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each is small or needs intent, and a pull request can change the guard itself"}, {"id": "docs_specs_0002_standards_and_tooling_rationale_heavy_decisions", "label": "Heavy decisions to review before accepting (3, 4, 5, 12, 27a, 28, 32)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/0002-standards-and-tooling/rationale.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_specs_0002_standards_and_tooling_rationale_evidence_gather